al Community (EPC) emerged as a crucial intergovernmental forum on October 6, 2022, during a summit held in Prague, Czech Republic, marking a concerted effort among European nations to address pressing political and strategic issues. This initiative stems from an increasing recognition of the need for collaboration in the face of contemporary challenges, such as the Russian invasion of Ukraine and the shifting global power dynamics. The EPC aims to encompass all 44 European countries, including members of the European Union and those outside it, thereby broadening the scope of political dialogue across the continent.

